How to Fix on GitHub Pages
1. Upload the logo

Put these files in your repository:

index.html
logo.png
2. Commit the changes

On GitHub:

Add logo.png
Add/update index.html
Commit changes
3. Check the image path

If the logo is in the root folder:

<img src="logo.png" alt="Logo">

If it's inside an images folder:

<img src="images/logo.png" alt="Logo">
4. Enable GitHub Pages

Go to:

Repository → Settings → Pages

Select:

Source: Deploy from a branch
Branch: main
Folder: /root

Save.

5. Wait 1–2 minutes

Your website will appear at:

https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/REPOSITORY-NAME/
Common GitHub Logo Problems

❌ Wrong:

<img src="C:\Users\Shafaat\Desktop\logo.png">

✅ Correct:

<img src="logo.png">

GitHub cannot access files on your computer; the image must be uploaded to the repository.

For a more professional look, I recommend using only the top logo mark (without the collage panels at the bottom) as the website logo. The full image you uploaded works better as a homepage banner or branding graphic than as a navigation/logo icon.
